    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/0AFB6B93B59D609A2037FAB5547D9B02/jobs/30220": {
      "title": "Financial Aid Counselor",
      "description": "Financial Aid Counselor You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Financial Aid Counselor Bronx, NY 10455 Apply Overview Salary Range $40,600.00 - $53,600.00 Salary Position Type Full Time Apply Description Metropolitan College of New York (MCNY) is a unique and vibrant learning institution.  It is a non-profit, regionally accredited college offering associate, bachelor's and master's degrees, with a state-of-the-art campus in the Hub district of the South Bronx.   For over 50 years, MCNY has offered highly motivated learners a powerful model of Purpose-Centered Education that promotes personal transformation and constructive change in workplaces and communities.  MCNY enrolls approximately 1,000 students annually into its accelerated degree programs with convenient onsite and remote schedules for added flexibility. Position Summary The Financial Aid Counselor is responsible for assisting students and their families in navigating the financial aid process, including applying for federal, state, and institutional aid. This position requires a strong understanding of financial aid regulations, excellent customer service skills, and the ability to provide accurate guidance on policies, procedures, and available funding options. This role requires interaction with students, families, and colleagues in both individual and group settings. Occasional evenings or weekends may be required for special events or peak processing times. Key Responsibilities: Counsel students and families regarding financial aid eligibility, application procedures, and available aid programs. Review and process financial aid applications in compliance with federal, state, and institutional policies. Utilize the PowerFAIDS system to manage student records, package aid, and generate reports. Interpret and apply regulations and policies from the U.S. Department of Education and other governing agencies. Monitor student eligibility, satisfactory academic progress, and compliance with financial aid requirements. Collaborate with admissions, registrar, and student accounts offices to support student enrollment and retention. Assist with outreach activities such as orientations, financial aid workshops, and information sessions. Stay current with updates to federal and state regulations, institutional policies, and best practices in financial aid administration. Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree in education, business, finance, or a related field (preferred). Minimum of two years of experience in financial aid or a related area. Proficiency with the PowerFAIDS financial aid system required. Strong knowledge of Department of Education policies and procedures . Excellent communication, organizational, and problem-solving skills. Ability to work effectively with diverse populations in a fast-paced environment. Commitment to providing high-quality student service with attention to detail and accuracy. Qualified candidates should submit their required documents above or mail to Metropolitan College of New York, Human Resources, 463 E 149 th Street, Bronx, NY 10455. For more information about MCNY please visit the College’s website at www.mcny.edu MCNY is an Equal Opportunity Employer Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    },
    "https://www.paycomonline.net/v4/ats/web.php/portal/0AFB6B93B59D609A2037FAB5547D9B02/jobs/28734": {
      "title": "Adjunct",
      "description": "Adjunct You need to enable JavaScript to run this app. Careers Sign In Create Account Adjunct Bronx, NY 10455 Apply Overview Salary Range $3,150.00 - $3,150.00 Salary Position Type Part Time Apply Description For over 60 years, Metropolitan College of New York (MCNY) has maintained a tradition of offering highly motivated adult learners an education that combines applied skills with professional knowledge, fostering personal transformation and positive change in workplaces and communities. MCNY is a private, nonprofit college accredited by the Middle States Commission on Higher Education. The College is home to three schools: the Audrey Cohen School for Human Services and Education , the School for Business , and the School for Public Affairs and Administration . Recognized as both a Predominantly Black Institution (PBI) and a Hispanic Serving Institution (HSI), MCNY is dedicated to serving a significant percentage of students of color, particularly from underrepresented communities. Founded in 1964 by Audrey Cohen, an educational visionary and activist, MCNY’s mission has remained steadfast, emphasizing Purpose-Centered Education to empower students to achieve their academic and professional goals. School for Business Description School for Business is one of the three schools at MCNY overseeing the MS in Project Management program and the course sections within the program. The selected adjunct professor will be serving under the School for Business in collaboration with other collegewide internal stakeholders. This is a part-time position for an Adjunct Professor at MCNY, based in the New York City Metropolitan area (Bronx) for on campus, in-person teaching in the evening from Monday through Thursdays . The Adjunct Professor(s) will be responsible for teaching project management courses within MS in Project Management program. For an overview of the MS in Project Management and the courses within the program, visit https://www.mcny.edu/academics/school-for-business/ms-project-management/course-offerings/ . Key Duties and Responsibilities Course Management - The Adjunct Professor will also be responsible, under the guidance and supervision of the Associate Dean, School for Business, for updating syllabus, updating the LMS (Moodle course shell) course contents and updating course materials preferably with Open Education Resources (OER). Student Support - Allocate regular office hours and provide academic support to ensure student success. Engagement - Foster active learning in a face-to-face setting. Administration - Timely student feedback, grading assignments, tests, discussion forums, timely submitting final grades and attendance records, and participate in School for Business assessment activities including CQI (Continuous Quality Improvement). Required Qualifications Education: Master's degree in Business Administration, Management, Project Management; however, candidates with doctoral degree and PMI project management certification(s) and relevant project management experience in similar fields of expertise will be preferred. Experience: Previous college-level teaching in project management and practical project managing experience is required; experience working with diverse student populations is preferred. Skills: Excellent communication, interpersonal, and pedagogical skills. Other Qualifications Expertise in a relevant field, as demonstrated by advanced degrees, publications, or work experience Excellent interpersonal and communication skills Ability to work collaboratively with colleagues and administrators Experience with online teaching and learning management system (LMS) platforms is desirable A commitment to social justice and equity, as evidenced by previous teaching or volunteer work in the community, is desirable Application Process Candidates should submit a CV/resume, a cover letter detailing teaching philosophy, education, experience and contact information for professional references.  Applications are generally accepted on an ongoing basis to build a hiring pool. Qualified candidates should submit their cover letter and resume above or mail to Metropolitan College of New York, Human Resources, 463 East 149th Street Bronx, NY 10455 For more information about MCNY please visit the College’s website at www.mcny.edu MCNY is an Equal Opportunity Employer Terms of Use | Privacy Policy | © 2026 Paycom | All Rights Reserved. X This website uses cookies to customize and improve your experience. If you are a California resident, you may be entitled to certain rights regarding your personal information. Additional information about our data collection practices and location specific notices is available on our privacy policy. Accept Cookies"
    }
